From: Robertas Tumas <robertas.t@8devices.com>
Subject: [PATCH] network access: SSH command whitelist, no login without a password, password policy, HTTPS

What a device offers over the network before and after its first
password is set.

- SSH: every session, interactive or "ssh host <cmd>", goes through a
  dropbear ForceCommand (uci-default 53-ssh-jail, all dropbear
  instances) running /usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh through sh (so it does not
  depend on the file mode), a whitelist that
  executes exactly reboot, jffs2reset and firstboot, single-letter
  options only, from /sbin; anything else is refused and an
  interactive session gets a one-line prompt for the same commands. No
  shell is handed to the client, so there is nothing to escape from and
  no file access of any kind (no scp/sftp). RED did this from
  /etc/profile, which only login shells read, so "ssh host <command>"
  bypassed it; a first port used rbash as a forced command, which
  still allowed reading any file through input redirection and needed
  the bash package. Privileged work is done on the console with sudo.
- rpcd (package patch): a login to an account without a password is
  refused. Upstream accepts any password for such an account so that a
  fresh device can be logged into; that gave anyone on the LAN a full
  session through LuCI or the ubus HTTP endpoint until the operator set
  a password, and a UI-level redirect cannot cover /ubus. The initial
  password is set through the LuCI first-login page (8devices luci
  series) or on the console (initial-password.sh) instead.
- Password policy: uci-default 52-password-policy enables the upstream
  rpcd policy with pw_length=8; LuCI's form reads it and the 8devices
  luci series enforces it server-side in setPassword, so it holds for
  the LuCI and ubus paths (busybox passwd on a root shell is not
  covered, as in RED).
- HTTPS: uci-default 54-https-redirect sets uhttpd redirect_https=1 when
  px5g (luci-ssl, in every 8devices config) is present, so the login
  form and session cookie never travel in clear; without px5g the
  redirect is not set, since it would point at a dead port.

Ported from lab.8devices.com/red/openwrt commits "drop to restricted
bash under SSH" and "jail.d: add firstboot symlink" (policy: jail for
every SSH user, root allowed over SSH but not on serial, unchanged);
the rpcd change, the policy-as-configuration and the HTTPS redirect are
new.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Robertas Tumas <robertas.t@8devices.com>
---
 .../files/etc/uci-defaults/52-password-policy      |  9 ++++
 .../base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/53-ssh-jail  | 10 +++++
 .../files/etc/uci-defaults/54-https-redirect       | 10 +++++
 package/base-files/files/usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh   | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 ...001-session-refuse-login-without-password.patch | 21 ++++++++++
 5 files changed, 98 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/52-password-policy b/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/52-password-policy
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..78e42da06d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/52-password-policy
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# 8devices CRA/RED: enable the LuCI/rpcd password policy with an 8-character
+# minimum. The LuCI form reads it, and the rpcd "luci" plugin enforces it
+# server-side (8devices luci series). Only meaningful where rpcd is installed.
+[ -f /etc/config/rpcd ] || exit 0
+uci -q get rpcd.policy >/dev/null || uci set rpcd.policy=policy
+uci set rpcd.policy.enabled='1'
+uci set rpcd.policy.pw_length='8'
+uci commit rpcd
+exit 0
diff --git a/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/53-ssh-jail b/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/53-ssh-jail
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..87b589e047
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/53-ssh-jail
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# 8devices CRA/RED: confine every SSH session to the restricted shell
+# (/usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh) by making it dropbear's forced command.
+# Run through sh, so it works whatever the file mode. Applied to all
+# dropbear instances present at first boot.
+[ -f /etc/config/dropbear ] || exit 0
+for s in $(uci -q show dropbear | sed -n 's/^dropbear\.\([^.=]*\)=dropbear$/\1/p'); do
+	uci -q set "dropbear.$s.ForceCommand=/bin/sh /usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh"
+done
+uci -q commit dropbear
+exit 0
diff --git a/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/54-https-redirect b/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/54-https-redirect
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..f002a8a8a6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/uci-defaults/54-https-redirect
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# 8devices CRA/RED: serve LuCI over TLS only. uhttpd generates a self-signed
+# certificate at first start when px5g (luci-ssl) is present; redirect plain
+# HTTP to it so that credentials and session cookies never travel in clear.
+# Images without px5g keep plain HTTP, since a redirect to a dead port would
+# lock the web UI out.
+[ -f /etc/config/uhttpd ] || exit 0
+[ -x /usr/sbin/px5g ] || exit 0
+uci -q set uhttpd.main.redirect_https='1'
+uci -q commit uhttpd
+exit 0
diff --git a/package/base-files/files/usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh b/package/base-files/files/usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..bf86715b7d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/base-files/files/usr/libexec/ssh-jail.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# 8devices CRA/RED: forced command for every SSH session, set as dropbear
+# "ForceCommand" by /etc/uci-defaults/53-ssh-jail. Only the commands listed
+# in $allowed may run, each with single-letter options only; nothing else is
+# interpreted. A remote command ("ssh host reboot") is checked and executed,
+# an interactive session gets a one-line prompt accepting the same commands.
+# No shell is ever handed to the client, so there is nothing to escape from
+# and no file can be read or written through it. Privileged work is done on
+# the serial console with sudo.
+allowed="reboot jffs2reset firstboot"
+
+run() {
+	local cmd a
+	set -f
+	# shellcheck disable=SC2086  # word splitting is the point, globbing is off
+	set -- $1
+	cmd=$1
+	[ $# -gt 0 ] && shift
+	case " $allowed " in
+		*" $cmd "*) ;;
+		*)
+			echo "ssh-jail: '$cmd' is not permitted (allowed: $allowed)" >&2
+			return 1
+			;;
+	esac
+	for a in "$@"; do
+		case $a in
+			-[a-zA-Z]) ;;
+			*)
+				echo "ssh-jail: argument '$a' is not permitted" >&2
+				return 1
+				;;
+		esac
+	done
+	"/sbin/$cmd" "$@"
+}
+
+if [ -n "$SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND" ]; then
+	run "$SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND"
+	exit $?
+fi
+
+echo "Restricted session. Commands: $allowed (Ctrl-D to leave)."
+while printf '> ' && IFS= read -r line; do
+	[ -n "$line" ] && run "$line"
+done
+echo
+exit 0
diff --git a/package/system/rpcd/patches/001-session-refuse-login-without-password.patch b/package/system/rpcd/patches/001-session-refuse-login-without-password.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..13b01af5aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/system/rpcd/patches/001-session-refuse-login-without-password.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+diff --git a/session.c b/session.c
+index 2dbc13b..7f1df4b 100644
+--- a/session.c
++++ b/session.c
+@@ -821,10 +821,14 @@ rpc_login_test_password(const char *hash, const char *password)
+ {
+ 	char *crypt_hash;
+ 
+-	/* password is not set */
++	/* password is not set: refuse the login. Upstream accepts any
++	 * password for an account without one so that a fresh device can
++	 * be logged into; on an 8devices CRA image the initial password is
++	 * set through the LuCI first-login page (as root, without a session)
++	 * or on the console, so no session may exist until then. */
+ 	if (!hash || !*hash)
+ 	{
+-		return true;
++		return false;
+ 	}
+ 
+ 	/* password hash refers to shadow/passwd */
